Required atSigns for deployment:

@owner_sign — The human owner. Used to authenticate, send commands, approve HITL actions, and define policies. Created at atsign.com.

@agent_sign — The AI agent itself. Its identity for all communication. Owns the encrypted memory store and audit logs.

@bridge_whatsapp, @bridge_telegram, @bridge_discord, @bridge_slack — One per messaging platform bridge. Relay-only policy, cannot execute commands.

@skill_calendar, @skill_email, @skill_files, @skill_[custom] — One per installed skill. Each scoped to its declared capabilities.

@mcp_home, @mcp_db, @mcp_browser, @mcp_[custom] — One per MCP server. Each with its own encrypted channel and tool allowlist.

Total for a typical deployment: 8-15 atSigns. Each is provisioned via Atsign Developer Starter Pack or programmatically via atSDK.

All atSigns are registered and provisioned BEFORE the system starts. The atPlatform ensures no component can operate without a valid, cryptographically verified identity.
